good morning believe nation today's  message is focused on the journey open  to you Jessie J I don't ever disregard  the fact that however hard you work you  know it doesn't always guarantee it's  gonna happen and that's the thing that  you have to just believe if you don't  believe in you no one else will even  bother to look at you and I shoved  myself around any open mics any gigs and  exactly an amount of stuff I've probably  done even up to now 80 90 % of all my  gigs for free surround yourself with  people that you can trust  surround us other people that let me be  you don't ever comes like compromise but  don't ever you know lose what makes you  you right from the heart stay happy and  always remember there's always someone  worse afternoon  and there's always someone that's  working lighter than you as well when  you're asleep there's someone roughed in  and that's what you have to remember as  well that for every 10 CDs you send off  there's someone sending over on 400 just  get yourself out there's much you can  and film everything  one thing I've learned that I'm glad  that I did footage from years ago that  people say to me oh you you've copied so  insane you've done you've done that I'm  like go on YouTube new fighters go still  the same songs are the same haircut it's  just you gotta have fun as well write it  down make sure you write down take  pictures and make sure it's a journey  and the journey is way more important  than where you end where you end up one  of the most popular questions I get  asked is how will I know when I've  reached 1 billion entrepreneurs  my big goal my big vision mission what I  want to do I want to reach a billion  entrepreneurs I want to know that I'm  having that kind of impact and put out  content and create amazing things for a  ton of entrepreneurs and I get people  asking well how will you know when you  hit a billion entrepreneurs or I don't  think there's even a billion  entrepreneurs in the world and you're  missing the point I don't actually have  a way to track if I'm hitting a billion  entrepreneurs and I don't care about it  because I'm not focused on the goal I'm  focused on the journey  what it does is make sure that it aligns  me to think about big projects and so  anything that I'm spending significant  time on I want to make sure has the  ability to reach a lot of people so I'm  making youtube videos because it can  spread and reach a lot of people when I  started to write my book I wanted to do  it with a big publisher not just  self-published even though  self-publishing can make me a lot more  money I want the big publisher because I  wanted to try to get more reach it's the  reason why I don't do business coaching  and one-on-one consulting although it  could be really meaningful and great to  have the one-on-one connection I want to  do things on a bigger scale and so what  that big goal allows me to do is focus  my efforts on the right projects but I  don't actually care about hitting a  billion entrepreneurs just like if I say  my next goal on the YouTube channels I  want to hit a million subscribers it's  amazing it's great you know you get a  play button we might have you know  another celebration but as soon as I hit  a goal  I don't really celebrate I feel like I  need to celebrate more because my team  it's a good thing to do kind of for  team-building but as soon as I hit a  goal I'm on to the next thing I don't  take time to celebrate because the work  is the celebration for me I want to work  more I want to get better I want to  continue to improve hitting a goal and  then saying that's it is death for me  and for a lot of people when you hit a  goal it actually be depressing you know  when I sold my first business it was 22  years old it was a great high great I  sold the company but then the next day I  had nothing to do like what do I weren't  supposed to do I got I'd have nothing to  go to in the morning and that's a great  problem to have and not something I'm  complaining about but still a problem  like when you hit a goal and you don't  know what you're gonna do next it's  depressing you don't know what to do  every day and when you don't have a plan  for what to do every day it can really  drag you down and so I think in doing  all these profiles of different famous  entrepreneurs people have had massive  success yes it can be great to have a  big goal it can be great to win an award  or hit a revenue target or lend that big  customer or whatever it is go IPO sell  your company have some big goal what if  the goal is the only thing  driving you it's gonna be really hard to  make it were the most successful people  the journey is the reward the journey of  creating something and marketing it and  you're getting better at it and seeing  the impact that is the work that is the  goal that is the joy that is the  excitement that is where you derive your  most pleasure from not just about  hitting some target and so it really  challenge you to look at your life your  business think about what your goals are  I love setting goals because when you  set a goal for me the most important  part of it is that it starts to align  your actions to achieve that goal and  it's not just about hitting the goal  it's about those actions those actions  are what's gonna serve me to be the best  version of me to allow me to have the  big impact that I want to have and so  look at your schedule look at what  you're doing every day look at your  day-in day-out in your business and in  your life do you enjoy the journey for  me getting married as an example I  didn't really care about the wedding day  Nina may not be too happy about that but  she knows I don't really care about the  wedding it's just another day like for  me the excitement the energy the joy is  in the marriage it's the everyday it's  the journey not just one day right when  you have a kid it's not just about the  kid being born and having the goal to  have a kid great amazing you know I've  hated almost eight years old that was an  amazing day but it's the it's journey  it's the day-to-day it's the parenting  it's every day connecting that's where  you grow and that's what you need to  enjoy if all you're waiting for as a  parent is for your kid to move out go to  college get a job if all you're waiting  for in your marriage is to hit that  ten-year anniversary your 25-year  anniversary your two-year anniversary or  whatever it it's like you're missing out  the goal is not as important as the  process to get there the goal helps you  align yourself so your actions help you  be the best version of you I'm not the  guy says no goals goals are important I  love having goals I set goals to myself  all the  but much more important than the goal is  the journey so the question today I love  your input what do you guys think is the  goal more important is the journey more  important share your thoughts give some  more context I'd love to hear what's on  your mind share it down the comments  below and we'll join in the conversation  I also want to give a quick shout it's a  gourd is Monde gourd thank you so much  for picking up a copy of my book your  one word it really really really really  means a lot to me and I hope you're  enjoying it thank you guys so much for  watching I believe in you I hope you  continue to believe in yourself and  whatever your one word is and I'll see  you again tomorrow morning for another  shot of espresso  [Music]

